TEST-001 structural-closure fix (QG cycle-3) -- kill verification
Generated 2026-08-08, sdd-forge-wt-phase4 worktree, branch feature/wave9-design-sync.

## Background

QG cycle-3 evaluator finding (T-001 re-review): the cycle-2 fix
(test001-class-fix.log) closed the two SPECIFIC syntactic shapes it named
(M6: a ':'-terminated branch definition appended to the Meaning cell; M7:
a ','+"value" prose sentence appended to the intro paragraph) by
enumerating them individually (AG_PS_COLON_TOKENS / AG_PS_COMMA_VALUE_TOKENS
in .sh; $agPsColonMatches / $agPsCommaValueMatches in .ps1). This closes
each named shape but not the class: a mutant naming a fourth value in any
OTHER shape -- e.g. a plain declarative sentence with neither a trailing
':' nor a nearby "value" word -- satisfies neither enumerated pattern and
still survives. Evaluator ruling: the whole scanned region currently
contains exactly 9 distinct backtick-quoted literals (standing,
per-feature, off, Standing, granted, ds_upload_consent, requirements.md,
design-sync-loop, Design-Source), so a set-equality ALLOWLIST over every
backtick literal in the region -- not just ones in a hand-picked syntactic
position -- closes the class structurally, with zero false positives on
the current text.

Separately (Major-2, same review): the cycle-2 Values-cell check
(AG_VALUES_NORM exact string match) is order-FIXED, but
acceptance-tests.md :85 only commits to "exactly three [values], in
either order" -- so the cycle-2 fix itself introduced a false positive on
a legitimately reordered but still-correct Values cell (e.g.
"`off` | `per-feature` | `standing`").

## Fix

1. Replaced the two-shape enumeration (AG_PS_COLON_TOKENS /
   AG_PS_COMMA_VALUE_TOKENS / AG_PS_BRANCH_TOKENS / case-folded compare)
   with an allowlist over ALL backtick-quoted literals found anywhere in
   the same scanned region (AG_PS_ROW_SCAN, unchanged: the section's own
   intro paragraph + the setting's own key row, table header/separator
   rows excluded). AG_PS_ALL_TOKENS (every backtick literal, case-
   sensitive, NOT folded -- `Standing` is kept as its own distinct
   allowlist entry rather than folded into `standing`, since folding is
   exactly what would let a genuinely different literal of another case
   hide behind an allowlist entry of a different case) must (a) be a
   subset of the current 9-literal allowlist (AG_PS_EXTRA_TOKENS empty)
   and (b) be a superset of {standing, per-feature, off}
   (AG_PS_HAS_ALL_THREE). Any new backtick literal, in ANY shape, now
   fails (a); dropping any of the three required values fails (b).
2. Replaced the Values-cell exact-string match (AG_VALUES_NORM) with an
   order-independent set comparison (AG_VALUES_SEGMENTS_SET, each `@ESC@`-
   delimited segment individually trimmed then sorted, compared against
   AG_VALUES_SEGMENTS_EXPECTED) -- still requires exactly 3 segments, each
   exactly one of the three literals, just no longer requires a specific
   left-to-right order.
3. TEST-001's own label text updated to drop "whole-section" (inaccurate:
   the scan was never the whole section, only the intro + key row) in
   favour of "order-independent Values-cell set + intro/key-row backtick-
   literal allowlist".

.ps1 mirror: $agPsAllTokens/$agPsAllowlist/$agPsRequiredThree (all
HashSet[string], case-sensitive default comparer) with .IsSubsetOf() for
both directions (avoids this file's barred Sort-Object, per its own
header discipline); $agValuesSegmentsSet/$agValuesSegmentsExpected
(HashSet + SetEquals) for the order-independent Values-cell check. No
Select-String, [regex] static method, switch -wildcard/-regex, or
Sort-Object introduced -- confirmed by grep sweep of the finished file
(only pre-existing header-comment/self-referential mentions remain).

Files touched: tests/design-sync-standing-consent.tests.sh (TEST-001
setup block + conditional) and tests/design-sync-standing-consent.tests.ps1
(TEST-001 setup block + conditional). No other file touched.

